Style the strip in a muted brand tone with the same ink border, and slide it under the sticky category chips so it never covers content. Keep the message reassuring, not alarmist ('saved menu', not 'no connection'). Pair with the SW cache-version bump discipline from the service-worker pattern so 'last updated' is always truthful — when you bump V you also update the stamp.

HTML: <header class="brew-hero"><div class="brew-stage"><svg class="mark">…animated mark…</svg><div class="steam"></div><h1 class="ar">بيت</h1><h1 class="en">BEYT</h1></div></header> then normal <section> categories below. CSS: give the hero a tall scroll runway and pin the stage —
.brew-hero{height:200vh}
.brew-stage{position:sticky;top:0;height:100vh;display:grid;place-items:center;animation:heroPlay linear both;animation-timeline:view();animation-range:entry 0% cover 60%}
@keyframes heroPlay{0%{opacity:0;transform:scale(1.15)}20%{opacity:1;transform:scale(1)}100%{opacity:1;transform:scale(.82)}}
.mark{animation:markBuild linear both;animation-timeline:view(root);animation-range:cover 0% cover 35%}
.steam{animation:rise linear infinite 3s} /* steam loops on its own time-timeline */
Name crossfade AR/EN is two <h1>s each with their own animation-range window. Guard everything: @supports not (animation-timeline: view()){ .brew-stage{position:static;height:auto;opacity:1;transform:none} } and @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ *{animation:none!important} }. Bilingual: on <html dir="rtl"> just swap which <h1> is visible via [dir] selectors; the scroll math is direction-agnostic.

Steam (CSS only): .steam span{position:absolute;bottom:100%;width:8px;height:34px;background:var(--ink);opacity:.15;filter:blur(6px);border-radius:50%;animation:rise 3s ease-in infinite}.steam span:nth-child(2){animation-delay:1s;left:14px} @keyframes rise{0%{transform:translateY(0) scaleX(1);opacity:.18}100%{transform:translateY(-40px) scaleX(2.4);opacity:0}}. Fill: draw the cup as SVG with a <rect class="coffee"> and mask it, then drive height by scroll —
.coffee{transform-origin:bottom;transform:scaleY(var(--fill,0));transition:transform .1s}
Native path: .signature{animation:pour linear both;animation-timeline:view();animation-range:entry 20% cover 55%}@keyframes pour{to{--fill:1}} (register with @property --fill{syntax:'<number>';initial-value:0;inherits:true} so it interpolates). Fallback path: IntersectionObserver + onscroll compute ratio = clamp((vh - rectTop)/vh) and el.style.setProperty('--fill',ratio). Price stamp: when --fill≈1 add a .stamped class that runs a quick scale-bounce keyframe. Gate the whole thing behind prefers-reduced-motion:reduce → show cup already full, no steam.
